# Copy to .env and edit. .env is Git-ignored; this file is not.
#
# Where `npm run test-vault:update` and `npm run export` install the built
# plugin. The folder must already be an Obsidian vault — the installer refuses
# anything without an .obsidian directory, so a mistyped path fails instead of
# scattering plugin files somewhere unexpected.
#
# Only test-vault/ is ever seeded or reset. A vault named here is an install
# target and nothing else, so `npm run test-vault:reset` cannot touch it.
#
# Takes precedence over the .project-weave-test-vault pointer file, and an
# explicit variable on the command line takes precedence over this file:
#
#   PROJECT_WEAVE_TEST_VAULT="/path/to/other/vault" npm run test-vault:update
#
# Windows paths work with either separator; quote a path containing spaces.
PROJECT_WEAVE_TEST_VAULT=/Users/you/Vaults/Project Weave Testing
